From a91e3db1f6b8fd58a9a308ed6225d82a151b0cf4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: will <will-tm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:30:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 36/36] hw/misc: imx.pwm, and the flintstone's piezo on PWM1

The Display-3.4 clicks through a piezo on PWM1 (fdt pwm-beeper, enable
on GPIO1_IO05, active low): nlclient plays a click as a 2 kHz tone for
3 ms (product.config clickfrequency/clickduration), through the input
driver onto pwm-imx. PWM1-4 were an unimplemented region, so the driver
wrote into nothing and the unit was silent.

Model the i.MX27-style PWM the 4.1 pwm-imx v2 path programs: PWMCR (a
software reset completes before the next read), PWMSR (the sample FIFO
takes each write at once, so it reads empty), PWMIR, PWMSAR, PWMPR. Its
"tone" output carries the frequency the pin toggles at, clock /
(prescaler + 1) / (period + 2), 0 while it is still; the clock is the
kernel's perclk, the 24 MHz oscillator. PWM1-4 join the i.MX6SX; 5-8
stay unimplemented.

flintstone.board reports PWM1 as BEEPER (the level in Hz, guest-time
stamped, so a listener can play a click for exactly as long) and the
enable as BEEPER-EN.
